WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.920
Usage specs are not checked in to my git

2
00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:07.600
repository. So when I pull down a

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.080
project from scratch, I need to make

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.480
sure I reinstall my usage specs so that

5
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.320
I can continue developing effectively.

6
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.800
I'll show this being done alongside the

7
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.840
usual npm install ritual purely because

8
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.680
it's a comparable process.

9
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.240
I have all the information in my package

10
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.039
JSON and tessle JSON to pull down both

11
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.000
my application dependencies and usage

12
00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:32.320
specs respectively. Like my node modules

13
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.320
folder, I don't add my actual usage

14
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.399
specs into my git repository. So I need

15
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.399
to reinstall both before my project is

16
00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:40.239
set up.

17
00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:43.040
I'll do this from my terminal, but I

18
00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:44.399
could also ask my agent. I'll run npm

19
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.800
install to download my library

20
00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:50.640
dependencies followed by tessle registry

21
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.719
install to download my usage specs.

22
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.960
Now we can see we have a node modules

23
00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.600
folder containing my dependencies as

24
00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.079
well as a usage specs folder under the

25
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.320
tzle directory holding all my usage

26
00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:03.920
specs.

27
00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.280
You've now reinstalled all the usage

28
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.280
specs and are ready for further

29
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.280
development.
